      <marc:subfield code="a">Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) is a planned 3-line mass rapid transit system in the Greater Kuala Lumpur conurbation in Malaysia. It envisages a &quot;wheel and spoke&quot; concept comprising two northwest-southeast radial lines and one circle line looping around Kuala Lumpur. The new MRT system is envisaged to radically improve and transform Kuala Lumpur’s poor and sorely inadequate public transportation coverage and to propel the Greater Kuala Lumpur metropolitan area to be on par with that of a developed city.</marc:subfield>
